op('rareaccuracy','Negative Positive','Accuracy Recall','[p[0]/(p[0]+p[1]),0]',lambda p:[p[0]/(p[0]+p[1]),0],'A toy population has {Negative} negative and {Positive} positive cases. A classifier predicts negative for everyone. What accuracy does it achieve?','An always-negative classifier can have high accuracy while detecting no positive cases. The class base rate supplies the apparent success.','grid')
def returnwalk(p):
 d=int(p[1]);states={(0,)*d:1.0}
 for _ in range(int(p[0])):
  nxt={}
  for x,w in states.items():
   for i in range(d):
    for delta in [-1,1]:
     y=list(x);y[i]+=delta;y=tuple(y);nxt[y]=nxt.get(y,0)+w/(2*d)
  states=nxt
 return [states.get((0,)*d,0)]
op('returnwalk','Steps Dimension','AtOrigin','[(()=>{const d=p[1],origin=Array(d).fill(0).join(",");let states=new Map([[origin,1]]);for(let n=0;n<p[0];n++){const next=new Map();for(const [key,w] of states){const x=key.split(",").map(Number);for(let i=0;i<d;i++)for(const delta of [-1,1]){const y=[...x];y[i]+=delta;const k=y.join(",");next.set(k,(next.get(k)||0)+w/(2*d));}}states=next;}return states.get(origin)||0;})()]',returnwalk,'A toy lattice walk starts at the origin in Dimension {Dimension}; each step uniformly chooses one of 2d unit directions. What is the probability it is at the origin after exactly {Steps} steps?','Endpoint return at a fixed finite time differs from ever returning over an infinite future. This enumeration answers only the finite question.','grid')
